# Postgres connection string (Neon, or any Postgres instance). Get one at neon.tech.
# `connection_limit` matters here: Prisma opens its own connection pool per
# process/instance on top of whatever pooler the database provides (Neon's
# `-pooler` host is one). Leaving it unset (Prisma defaults to ~2x CPU cores)
# risks exhausting the database's real connection limit when many instances
# exist at once (many concurrent serverless invocations, or several `next
# dev` restarts in a row locally) — surfaces as "connection pool timeout"
# errors. But setting it to 1 serializes every concurrent request within a
# single process onto one connection, which is its own bug — unrelated
# requests (an upload, a feed poll, a create) start queueing behind each
# other, and everything feels slow. 5 is a reasonable middle ground for a
# small app: enough headroom for real concurrency within one process,
# low enough that several instances still can't exhaust the database.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require&connection_limit=5"

# Gates /admin (moderation queue, all-challenges view). Use a fresh, strong
# password in production — don't reuse this across environments.
ADMIN_PASSWORD="change-me"

# Optional. Enables Vercel Blob storage for video recordings — required in
# production (local disk doesn't work on Vercel's ephemeral filesystem).
# Auto-populated if you enable Blob storage on a Vercel project; leave unset
# locally to fall back to local-disk storage under public/uploads/.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""
